    "name": "Grandmother",
    "description": "Synthesizers\nAccessories\nSoftware Store\nThe Wave\nSupport\nSynthesizers\nAccessories\nSoftware Store\nThe Wave\nSupport\nFeatured Products\nMessenger\nSYNTHESIZERS\n\nA New Method Of Sonic Experimentation, Communication, And Connection Has Arrived\n\nDISCOVER\n\nLabyrinth\nSYNTHESIZERS\n\nHow Deep Does The Rabbit Hole Go? Meet Labyrinth, An Idea Machine That Aims To Answer That Very Question.\n\nDISCOVER\n\nGet The Latest Moog News\n\nThis site is protected by reCAPTCHA and the Google\nPrivacy Policy and Terms of Service apply.\n\nHome\n\n/\n\nSynthesizers\n\n/\n\nGrandmother\nGrandmother\n\nFind a Dealer\n\nPlayful, Powerful Tones and Textures\n\nGrandmother® is a semi-modular analog synthesizer with a built-in arpeggiator, sequencer and spring reverb tank.\n\nDownloads\n\nIntroduction\n\nOverview\n\nVideo\n\nSpecs\n\nResources\n\nWalkthroughs\n\n1\n2\n3\n4\n5\n6\n\nInspired By The Classic Moog Modular Synthesizers.\n\nGrandmother is a semi-modular analog synthesizer with a built-in arpeggiator, sequencer and spring reverb tank. Start playing immediately with “no patching required”, and then explore an infinite sonic playground with Grandmother’s reconfigurable front panel. Grandmother’s circuits, spring reverb, and spirit are inspired by the classic Moog Modular Synthesizers, making this instrument a powerful addition to a Mother-32, DFAM or any Eurorack modular system.\n\nAdrian Younge's Thesis On Sound\n\nTo explore the sonic possibilities and cosmic context of Grandmother, Moog Music visited the Linear Labs studio of artist-composer Adrian Younge (Black Dynamite, Netflix’s Luke Cage).\n\nIn this video, Younge gives his personal “Thesis On Sound” while incorporating Grandmother into his retro-inspired creative workflow at Linear Labs.\n\nRecord And Playback Sequences With Up To 256 Notes Each.\n\nGrandmother features an easy to use Arpeggiator and Sequencer for added enjoyment and programmable syncopation. \n\nAdd lush, expansive ambience to any sound.\n\nInspired by the classic Moog modular synthesizers that came before it, Grandmother's sound engine, modulation engine and onboard spring reverb tank are completely analog, resulting in an unrestricted sonic vocabulary of immeasurable beauty and power.\n\nExplore a vast array of sonic possibilities through analog interconnectivity.\n\nThough not required, creative patching and exploration are the keys to discovering exciting new relationships between modules and to truly unlocking Grandmother’s infinite expanse of auditory inspiration. Patching can also be used to override internal connections, allowing each section to function just as an independent module would.\n\n1\n2\n3\n\nGrandmother Specifications\n\nTYPE\n\nSemi-Modular Analog Synthesizer\n\nSOUND ENGINE\n\nAnalog\n\nNUMBER OF KEYS\n\n32 Full-Size Keys\n\nTYPE OF KEYS\n\nVelocity-sensing (Velocity signal is not hard-wired – available via MIDI and KBD VEL OUT jack)\n\nOTHER CONTROLLERS\n\nPitch Bend, Mod Wheel, Variable Glide\n\nPOLYPHONY\n\nMonophonic\n\nSOUND SOURCES\n\n2 Oscillators with selectable Waveforms (Oscillator 2 supports Sync to Oscillator 1 plus linear FM), 1 White Noise Generator, External Input jack\n\nSHOW FULL LIST +\n\nExplore Grandmother\n\nSynthesis is a journey and we hope that these resources help guide your explorations with Grandmother. On this page you will find a growing collection of tutorial videos, patchbooks, tips, and other helpful resources. Each artist's relationship with synthesis is unique and we hope that these guides can help inspire you to discover your own path.\n\nDownload the Grandmother Manual\n\nVideo Walkthroughs\n\nSequencer Basics\n\nWith Grandmother’s easy-to-use on-board sequencer, learn to quickly program and store up 3 different sequences, add variety with ties & rests, transpose patterns, and overdub new notes during playback.\n\nSequencer Basics\n\nIn this video we explore how to ping the filters of Spectravox to turn it into an analog physical modelling instrument and create percussive wooden sounds like marimbas or xylophones.\n\nBuilding Sequences Live\n\nThis video explores creative approaches to building sequences live using Grandmother.\n\nPatching the LFO as a Third Oscillator\n\nUsing Grandmother’s front panel patch points, you can easily reconfigure the instrument’s on-board analog LFO to act as a third oscillator.\n\nEnvelope-Controlled Oscillator Sync\n\nOscillator sync is a very unique feature found on synthesizers with two or more oscillators in their voice architecture.\n\n2-Op Analog FM Synthesis\n\nThis video explores how to achieve analog 2-operator FM synthesis using Grandmother.\n\nMulti Trig\n\nThis video explores the multi trig feature added in firmware v1.1.3 to Grandmother’s Global Settings.\n\nRecord Noise\n\nThis video explores a sound design technique found in 'PATCH & TWEAK with Moog' that allows users to generate a convincing vinyl record noise using Grandmother.\n\nLess Muddy Reverb\n\nThis video explores a signal flow technique found in 'PATCH & TWEAK with Moog' that adds some tonal control to Grandmother’s spring reverb, helping to improve clarity on bass-heavy patches.\n\nRandomized Filter Envelope Modulation\n\nThis video explores using Grandmother’s sample and hold circuit to create randomized envelope modulation of the filter.\n\nSynthesizers\n\nDISCOVER\n\nAccessories\n\nDISCOVER\n\nSoftware Store\n\nSHOP SOFTWARE\n\nSupport\nForum\nHelpdesk\nKnowledge base\nDownloads\nAll Product Downloads\nPresets\nUser Manuals\nPatches\nFirmware Updates\nThe Wave\nView all articles\nRSS Feed\nAbout Us\nCareers\nTerms Of Use\nPrivacy\nFind A Dealer\nGet The Latest Moog News\n\nThis site is protected by reCAPTCHA and the Google\nPrivacy Policy and Terms of Service apply.",
